{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.q_0_exists_in_universal_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.q_0_exists_in_universal_base","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L186-L194","doc":"**Conditional corollary**: the substrate parameter exists in any\nsufficient base ring. Demonstrates the Z[q, q⁻¹]-universal framing\nworks through the class structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.q_0_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.q_0_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L159-L184","doc":"**Conditional theorem**: under all the structural hypotheses above\n(Mostow-Prasad rigidity, Reid's trace field, and the q_0 identification),\nthe substrate is *well-defined* in the sense the word actually carries:\nit does not depend on which identification is chosen.  Two instances\nthat agree on the invariant map agree on `q_0`, because both are pinned\nto `traceInvariant ρ_DF` by `identification_witness`.\n\nSo the conjectural content sits entirely in whether an instance exists\n— exhibiting `traceInvariant` and proving the identity, which is the\nOPEN WORK — and none of it in ambiguity about `q_0` once one does.\n\nThe previous statement was `∃ q : R, q = inst.q_0`, proved\n`⟨inst.q_0, rfl⟩`.  That holds for any field of any structure and would\nhave been just as provable had `identification_witness` been dropped\nfrom the class, so it tested none of the hypotheses it was stated\nunder — the docstring's \"FULLY VERIFIED BY LEAN\" was true and\nuninformative at the same time.  Existence of an element is\n`q_0_exists_in_universal_base` below, which at least says `R` is\ninhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.identification_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.identification_witness","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L155-L155","doc":"**The identification**: `q_0` equals the invariant of the\ndistinguished discrete-faithful representation `ρ_DF`.  This is\nthe open conjectural content (`q_0 = traceInvariant [ρ_DF]`),\nnow a genuine equation rather than a `True` placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.traceInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.traceInvariant","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L150-L150","doc":"An algebraic invariant of a representation, valued in the\nsubstrate ring `R` (e.g. a trace-field / cusp-shape coordinate;\nfinite over `ℚ` by Reid's theorem, hence `R`-valued). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.q_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.q_0","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L146-L146","doc":"The substrate parameter, as an element of R. For our universe,\nR = R (real) and q_0 ≈ 1.1097; categorically R could be C, F_p,\netc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification.mk","kind":"ctor","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L140-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.QZeroStokesIdentification","kind":"class","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L128-L155","doc":"**The OPEN conjecture**: the specific algebraic identification of\nthe substrate $q_0$ as an invariant of $[\\rho_{\\mathrm{DF}}]$.\n\nThree candidate refinements (per the audit §11):\n  (a) Dehn-deformed structure → cusp coordinate on A-polynomial\n  (b) Longitude trace (not meridian, which is parabolic)\n  (c) Markov-trace parameterization\n\nThe class axiomatizes that SOME such identification exists,\nwithout committing to a specific form (the invariant map\n`traceInvariant` is abstract). Instance inhabitation — exhibiting\nthe invariant and proving the identity — is the OPEN WORK. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-zero-stokes-region-identification","label":"conj:q-zero-stokes-region-identification","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField.finite_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField.finite_positive","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L124-L124","doc":"Non-triviality: degree at least 1 (the field is Q itself for\ndegree = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField.trace_field_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField.trace_field_degree","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L121-L121","doc":"The degree of the trace field over Q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.ReidTraceField","kind":"class","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L111-L124","doc":"**Class axiomatization of Reid's trace-field theorem** (Reid 1990):\nthe trace field Q(tr ρ_DF) is a number field of finite degree\nover Q. Hence ρ_DF is defined over $\\overline{\\mathbb{Q}}$, NOT\nrequiring transcendental data.\n\nFor Borromean specifically: the trace field is conjecturally\n$\\mathbb{Q}(\\zeta_6) = \\mathbb{Q}(i\\sqrt{3})$ (or similar 3rd-root-of-\nunity-related). Concrete degree needs SnapPy verification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.rigid","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L109-L109","doc":"**Mostow–Prasad rigidity** (Mostow 1968, Prasad 1973): the\ndiscrete-faithful representation is unique up to conjugation —\nevery discrete-faithful `r` is conjugate to `ρ_DF`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.rho_DF_isDF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.rho_DF_isDF","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L105-L105","doc":"`ρ_DF` is discrete-faithful. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.rho_DF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.rho_DF","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The distinguished discrete-faithful representation `ρ_DF`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.IsDiscreteFaithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.IsDiscreteFaithful","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The discrete-faithful predicate: `r` is the holonomy of a complete\nfinite-volume hyperbolic structure on `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.Conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.Conjugate","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Conjugacy equivalence on representations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.Rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.Rep","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The representation variety of `π₁(K)` into `PSL₂(ℂ)` (abstract:\nthe concrete construction is not in Mathlib).  Universe-polymorphic\nso a later concrete `Rep` in any universe fits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.MostowPrasadDistinguished","kind":"class","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L79-L109","doc":"**Class axiomatization of Mostow-Prasad rigidity** (Mostow 1968 +\nPrasad 1973): for a finite-volume hyperbolic 3-manifold, the\ndiscrete-faithful representation π_1 → PSL_2(ℂ) is UNIQUE up to\nconjugation. The class instance asserts existence + uniqueness.\n\nStatus: literature-proved; Lean instance carries the conjectural\n\"this knot complement is hyperbolic of finite volume\" hypothesis.\n\nThe class abstracts the representation variety (`Rep`), the\nconjugation equivalence (`Conjugate`), and the discrete-faithful\npredicate (`IsDiscreteFaithful`) rather than the concrete\n`PSL₂(ℂ)`-machinery (not in Mathlib); `rigid` then states the actual\nMostow–Prasad uniqueness-up-to-conjugation claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.borromean","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L70-L73","doc":"The Borromean rings complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement.vol_over_G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement.vol_over_G","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Hyperbolic volume in units of Catalan's constant G. For B_3: 8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement.num_cusps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement.num_cusps","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Number of cusps. For B_3: 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.KnotComplement","kind":"structure","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L62-L68","doc":"An abstract knot complement as a Lean type. The Borromean rings\nB_3 is the canonical instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.q_inv_property","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.q_inv_property","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The defining relation `q · q⁻¹ = 1`.  Since `R` is commutative,\nthis genuinely witnesses that `q` is a unit\n(`isUnit_of_mul_eq_one q q_inv q_inv_property : IsUnit q`), matching\nthe `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` intent above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.q_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.q_inv","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Generator q⁻¹ as an element of R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.q","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Generator q as an element of R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QZeroStokesRegionIdentification.UniversalBase","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/q-zero-stokes-region-identification.lean#L45-L60","doc":"The universal base ring: $\\mathbb{Z}[q, q^{\\pm 1}]$ as an abstract\ncommutative ring. In Lean Mathlib this would be\n`LaurentPolynomial ℤ` (or `Polynomial.LaurentPolynomial ℤ`).\n\nMade abstract here to keep the file lightweight; an actual instance\ncan be supplied by importing Mathlib's LaurentPolynomial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}